Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-rs6000.c
Line: 1938
Function: xcoff_write_armap_old
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: The inner loop uses map[i] in its condition without re-checking that i < orl_count. Since i is incremented inside the loop, it can reach or exceed orl_count before the condition is re-evaluated, causing a read past the end of the map array (map[i].abfd) and potential crash or memory disclosure.

